---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AviationDashboard from "../../components/dashboard/AviationDashboard";
---

<BaseLayout title="Pakistan Aviation Analytics" description="Pakistan's most comprehensive public aviation traffic dashboard — 2006 to 2026">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16">
    <p class="strip-label">Data Flagship</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold">Pakistan Aviation Analytics</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-strip-muted">
      Pakistan's Civil Aviation Authority (CAA) publishes yearly airline, airport, passenger, and cargo statistics — traditionally as unstructured PDF reports that are difficult to search, compare, or analyse across time. This dashboard is the most comprehensive public interactive view of that data available anywhere: <strong class="text-strip-text">two decades of traffic records (2006–2026)</strong>, covering ~300M passenger movements and ~5.4M tonnes of cargo, exclusively accessible here as a cross-filterable BI tool.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {["Python ETL", "DuckDB-WASM", "Recharts", "KPI Design", "Data Validation"].map((t) => <span class="tag">{t}</span>)}
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 space-y-8">
      <div class="strip-card max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-strip-signal">Context</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-strip-muted">
          Government aviation data exists — but not in a form stakeholders can actually use. Yearly PDF releases make it nearly impossible to answer questions like "how did Karachi's international traffic recover post-COVID?" or "which domestic carrier grew fastest in the last five years?" without manual spreadsheet work.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="strip-card max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-strip-accent">Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-strip-muted">
          Built a Python ETL pipeline that cleans, validates, and structures 173K+ flight-leg records — including direction-aware Pakistani airport aggregation (so Karachi's traffic isn't silently halved) and Islamabad airport merge logic. Pre-aggregated JSON loads instantly; DuckDB-WASM enables client-side SQL for real cross-filtering without a backend server.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="strip-card max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-strip-text">Effect</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-strip-muted">
          The only place to explore two decades of Pakistan aviation traffic data interactively — filter by year, segment, airline, and airport; export subsets to CSV; and read analyst-grade insights baked into the dashboard. Partial-year flags on 2006 (H2 only) and 2026 (H1 YTD) prevent misleading trend interpretations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <AviationDashboard client:load />
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
